  <data key="d26">vibrational_density_of_states_calculation</data>
  <data key="d27">[]</data>
  <data key="d28">Two-phase thermodynamics model applied to reactive trajectories to generate vibrational densities of states for comparison with experimental spectroscopy.</data>
  <data key="d24">["calc_two_phase_thermodynamics_vdos"]</data>
  <data key="d25">1</data>
</node>
<node id="obs_distinguished_co2rr_intermediates">
  <data key="d21">ObservationClaim</data>
  <data key="d22">Reactive intermediates in the carbon dioxide reduction reaction were distinguished by resolving simulated vibrational signals for comparison with reported experimental spectroscopy.</data>
  <data key="d29">intermediate_identification</data>
  <data key="d30">Reactive intermediates in the carbon dioxide reduction reaction were distinguished by resolving simulated vibrational signals for comparison with reported experimental spectroscopy.</data>
  <data key="d31">computational</data>
  <data key="d23">The abstract reports successful distinction of reactive CO2RR intermediates using the solvent- and voltage-inclusive simulation workflow.</data>
  <data key="d24">["obs_distinguished_co2rr_intermediates"]</data>
  <data key="d25">1</data>
</node>
<node id="mech_atomic_scale_co2rr_understanding">
  <data key="d21">MechanismClaim</data>
  <data key="d22">Explicit consideration of solvent and applied voltage at the electrode–electrolyte interface enables reactive-trajectory and vibrational-signal analysis that provides atomic-scale understanding of the carbon dioxide reduction reaction.</data>
  <data key="d29">atomic_scale_mechanistic_understanding</data>
  <data key="d30">Explicit consideration of solvent and applied voltage at the electrode–electrolyte interface enables reactive-trajectory and vibrational-signal analysis that provides atomic-scale understanding of the carbon dioxide reduction reaction.</data>
  <data key="d31">computational</data>
  <data key="d23">This is the authors' stated interpretation of the operando QM simulation approach and its identification of reactive intermediates.</data>
  <data key="d24">["mech_atomic_scale_co2rr_understanding"]</data>
  <data key="d25">1</data>
</node>
